Z||000001||Oreif||01-08-2001||01:49 PM||||Typically the front and back should be the same. Does the pedal go to the floor the same way as it does when bleeding the rears? It could be M/C or a damaged/twisted/clogged hardline. I would think the way you descibe it that the fronts are somehow being restricted.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||01-08-2001||02:07 PM||||no, the pedal didn't seem to move as much when i opened the fronts.  especially when it was all foam.<P>it has to be a restriction, but the question is where?  master cylinder, line, or caliper?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-08-2001||07:36 PM||||sounds like one of the lines sucking air. check all the front lines. including all the steel line.<P>If it's both sides it could be the steel lines near the MC or even the prop/balance valve.||||reg||1
